 passage 2. \r\nChoose True or False. \r\nTrue- if the statement agrees with the information\r\nFalse- if the statement contradicts the information\r\nIncredible people are admired only for their luck, not for their talent or effort.',2.00,1,'2026-01-01 21:33:42','2026-01-05 11:52:06'),(674,61,3,'Talented musicians and athletes work hard for many years to improve their skills.',2.00,1,'2026-01-01 21:34:18','2026-01-05 11:52:18'),(675,61,3,'Respect is earned only by being talented, not through honesty or kindness.',2.00,1,'2026-01-01 21:34:35','2026-01-05 11:52:31'),(676,61,3,'Incredible people can inspire others to follow their dreams and never give up.',2.00,1,'2026-01-01 21:35:03','2026-01-05 11:52:43'),(677,61,3,'Everyone can learn from incredible people by studying their lives and trying to achieve their own goals.',2.00,1,'2026-01-01 21:35:32','2026-01-05 11:52:57'),(678,61,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 1.',2.00,1,'2026-01-01 21:37:27','2026-01-05 11:53:21'),(679,61,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 2.',2.00,1,'2026-01-01 21:37:50','2026-01-05 11:53:35'),(680,61,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 3',2.00,1,'2026-01-01 21:38:11','2026-01-05 11:53:48'),(681,61,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 4.',2.00,1,'2026-01-01 21:38:36','2026-01-05 11:54:02'),(682,61,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 5.',2.00,1,'2026-01-01 21:39:00','2026-01-05 11:54:13'),(683,62,3,'Do the following statements agree with the information given in reading passage 1. \r\nChoose True or False. \r\nTrue- if the statement agrees with the information\r\nFalse- if the statement contradicts the information\r\nLarry Page and Sergey Brin met at Stanford University before starting Google.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:01:27','2026-01-05 11:54:33'),(684,62,3,'Google’s first office was in a small garage before they moved to a larger space.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:01:59','2026-01-05 11:54:48'),(685,62,3,'Google Maps and Google Earth were introduced in different years.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:02:15','2026-01-05 11:55:01'),(686,62,3,'By 2006, the word “Google” had become a verb in English dictionaries, showing the company’s impact on modern life.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:02:35','2026-01-05 11:55:16'),(687,62,3,'Google only focuses on technology and does not support creativity in the community.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:03:22','2026-01-05 11:55:32'),(688,62,1,'Choose the correct letter A or B.\r\nWhat was Google’s original goal?',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:04:11','2026-01-05 11:55:49'),(689,62,1,'Who was Google’s first employee?',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:04:46','2026-01-05 11:56:02'),(690,62,1,'How many languages could people search in by 2000?',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:05:14','2026-01-05 11:56:26'),(691,62,1,'What project helps people explore museums online?',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:06:22','2026-01-05 11:56:41'),(692,62,1,'What is one future project Google was working on in 2018?',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:06:52','2026-01-05 11:56:55'),(693,62,3,'Complete the summary using the list of words.\r\nGoogle was started by two ____________ , Larry Page and Sergey Brin, who met at Stanford University.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:08:24','2026-01-05 11:57:15'),(694,62,3,'Their ___________  was to organize all of the information on the Web and make it easy for people to find.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:09:04','2026-01-05 11:57:28'),(695,62,3,'At first, they ________________  their company in a small garage and hired their first employee, Craig Silverstein.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:09:41','2026-01-05 11:57:45'),(696,62,3,'Over time, Google grew quickly and now __________________  more than 40,000 people around the world.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:10:16','2026-01-05 11:58:01'),(697,62,3,'The company not only provides a fast and smart search engine but also helps new businesses ____________ and find customers. Google encourages creativity among its employees and in the community, creating new products and projects that make life easier and more interesting.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:11:00','2026-01-05 11:58:19'),(698,63,3,'Do the following statements agree with the information given in reading passage 2. \r\nChoose True or False. \r\nTrue- if the statement agrees with the information\r\nFalse- if the statement contradicts the information\r\nSome people believe life could exist on other planets because there are many stars and planets.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:12:22','2026-01-05 11:58:56'),(699,63,3,'Exoplanets are planets that exist only in our solar system.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:12:54','2026-01-05 11:59:13'),(700,63,3,'Scientists study atmospheres and gases like oxygen to look for signs of life.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:13:26','2026-01-05 11:59:32'),(701,63,3,'Sending robots and spacecraft to distant planets is easy and fast.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:13:55','2026-01-05 11:59:45'),(702,63,3,'Even if life exists on other planets, it might be very different from life on Earth.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:14:22','2026-01-05 12:00:21'),(703,63,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 1.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:16:08','2026-01-05 12:00:41'),(704,63,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 2.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:16:58','2026-01-05 12:01:08'),(705,63,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 3.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:17:24','2026-01-05 12:01:28'),(706,63,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 4.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:18:09','2026-01-05 12:01:50'),(707,63,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 5.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:18:49','2026-01-05 12:02:16'),(708,67,3,'Carol Dweck believes that recent research on intelligence is helping us better understand how students think.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:36:23','2026-01-06 12:03:54'),(709,67,3,'Students with a fixed mindset usually enjoy challenges and feel motivated by setbacks.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:36:38','2026-01-06 12:04:07'),(710,67,3,'Dweck says that people with a fixed mindset often see mistakes as a sign that they are not intelligent.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:37:01','2026-01-06 12:04:19'),(711,67,3,'According to the passage, a growth mindset means believing that intelligence can increase through effort.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:37:20','2026-01-06 12:04:38'),(712,67,3,'Dweck claims that students with a growth mindset begin to enjoy learning because they trust only their natural talent.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:37:38','2026-01-06 12:04:48'),(713,67,1,'Read the quotes from the reading. Choose the statement that explains each quote.\r\n“These different beliefs create different attitudes.” (Paragraph 2)',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:38:32','2026-01-06 12:06:09'),(714,67,1,'“A fixed mindset makes challenges threatening for people.” (Paragraph 3)',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:39:34','2026-01-06 12:06:28'),(715,67,1,'“Everyone has different abilities, and not everyone can be as smart as Einstein.” (Paragraph 4)',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:40:20','2026-01-06 12:06:43'),(716,67,1,'“Confronting challenges, profiting from mistakes, and persevering… help people to become smarter.” (Paragraph 4)',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:40:56','2026-01-06 12:07:01'),(717,67,1,'“It is preferable to react to them in a constructive, determined way.” (Paragraph 5)',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:41:33','2026-01-06 12:07:15'),(718,67,3,'Complete the summary using the list of words.\r\nThe passage discusses Carol Dweck’s research on how students’ beliefs about intelligence affect their motivation and learning. Students with a fixed mindset often see intelligence as unchangeable, so when they face challenges or experience  _________________ ,',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 10:42:53','2026-01-06 12:07:30'),(719,67,3,'they may feel ______________ and lose confidence. They interpret mistakes as signs of low ability, which makes progress difficult. In contrast, students with a growth mindset believe that intelligence can develop through effort and practice.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 11:17:16','2026-01-06 12:07:45'),(720,67,3,'They interpret mistakes as signs of low ability, which makes progress difficult. In contrast, students with a growth mindset believe that intelligence can develop through effort and practice. This belief encourages them to respond to difficulties in a  __________________ way.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 11:17:59','2026-01-06 12:07:59'),(721,67,3,'Instead of giving up, they remain __________________ , learn from their mistakes, and continue working toward improvement.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 11:18:40','2026-01-06 12:08:12'),(722,67,3,'According to Dweck, this positive approach to learning leads to greater resilience and higher _________________  in the long run.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:36:48','2026-01-06 12:08:24'),(723,68,3,'Do the following statements agree with the information given in reading passage 2. \r\nChoose True or False. \r\nTrue- if the statement agrees with the information\r\nFalse- if the statement contradicts the information\r\n\r\nDrinking water before meals can help people eat less food.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:38:56','2026-01-06 12:09:09'),(724,68,3,'Water slows down the body’s metabolism and reduces calorie burning.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:39:14','2026-01-06 12:09:22'),(725,68,3,'Choosing water instead of sugary drinks can reduce daily calorie intake.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:39:37','2026-01-06 12:09:37'),(726,68,3,'Being well-hydrated can improve physical performance during exercise.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:39:54','2026-01-06 12:09:48'),(727,68,3,'Water alone is enough to replace a healthy diet and regular exercise for weight loss.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:40:23','2026-01-06 12:10:00'),(728,68,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 1.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:41:36','2026-01-06 12:10:24'),(729,68,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 2.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:42:33','2026-01-06 12:10:57'),(730,68,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 3.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:43:05','2026-01-06 12:10:37'),(731,68,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 4.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:44:11','2026-01-06 12:11:12'),(732,68,3,'Choose the correct heading for paragraph 5.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:45:07','2026-01-06 12:11:34'),(733,68,3,'Complete the summary using the list of words.\r\nDrinking enough water plays an important role in ______________ weight loss.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:46:57','2026-01-06 12:12:29'),(734,68,3,'Water supports many body functions, including digestion and metabolism, which helps the body use energy more ____________',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:47:39','2026-01-06 12:12:02'),(735,68,3,'When people drink water before or during meals, they often feel fuller and eat less, which can _____________________ their overall calorie intake without feeling hungry.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:48:17','2026-01-06 12:12:44'),(736,68,3,'Water can also slightly _______________ calorie burning and support long-term weight control.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:49:01','2026-01-06 12:13:03'),(737,68,3,'In addition, choosing water instead of sugary drinks helps people avoid extra sugar and calories that can lead to weight _________ Finally, proper hydration keeps the body energized and active, making exercise easier and more effective, and helping people reach their weight-loss goals in a healthy way.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:49:33','2026-01-06 12:13:20'),(738,69,3,'Do the following statements agree with the information given in reading passage 1.  (5 points)\r\nChoose True or False. \r\n\r\nTrue- if the statement agrees with the information\r\nFalse- if the statement contradicts the information\r\n\r\nOne reason robotic surgery is useful is that robots do not lose focus during long or repetitive procedures',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:56:38','2026-01-06 12:14:03'),(739,69,3,'Human simulators only prepare medical students for simple medical situations, not serious emergencies',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:56:56','2026-01-06 12:14:12'),(740,69,3,'Some robotic mannequins can show physical reactions such as sweating or bleeding.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:57:19','2026-01-06 12:14:22'),(741,69,3,'Robots help nurses mainly because they can move patients more safely than humans who may become tired.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:57:37','2026-01-06 12:14:43'),(742,69,3,'The patient who used robotic pants said his daughter immediately began talking excitedly when she saw him walking again.',1.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:57:52','2026-01-06 12:14:53'),(743,69,1,'Read the quotes from the reading. Choose the statement that explains each quote.  \r\n“There are millions of robots in use throughout the world.” (Paragraph 1)',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:58:43','2026-01-06 12:16:25'),(744,69,1,'“They operate on patients without having to be in the same physical location.” (Paragraph 2)',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:59:10','2026-01-06 12:17:25'),(745,69,1,'“These pieces of equipment not only resemble real people, but they also act like them.” (Paragraph 3)',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 12:59:49','2026-01-06 12:17:44'),(746,69,1,'“A common problem in hospitals is that nurses constantly have to move people from one bed to another.” (Paragraph 4)',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 13:00:24','2026-01-06 12:18:05'),(747,69,1,'“The pants have advantages that are not only physical.” (Paragraph 5)',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 13:01:01','2026-01-06 12:34:41'),(748,69,3,'Complete the summary using the list of words.\r\nRobots play an increasingly important role in modern health care because they provide many ______________________ to doctors, nurses, and patients.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 13:03:14','2026-01-06 12:20:22'),(749,69,3,'In surgery, robots can perform delicate and 12) ___________  tasks without becoming 13)  __________ , which makes operations more accurate and may help patients heal faster.',4.00,1,'2026-01-02 13:15:36','2026-01-06 12:31:48'),(750,69,3,'Medical students also train with advanced simulators that look and act like real people; these mannequins can sweat, react to drugs, and even ______________ giving students a safe way to practice difficult emergency situations.',2.00,1,'2026-01-02 13:16:46','2026-01-06 12:24:13'),(751,69,3,'Robots support nurses as well by lifting and moving patients, lowering the risk of _______